comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T00:20:30.191Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all statuses for provenance value-domain, immutable legacy, strict health, advisory policy, and single-digit role. pm-eq9dlw owns detection and the original resolver defect; this distinct downstream verdict/disposition gap was reproduced in pm-changelog PR #138 after adopting pm-cli 2026.8.11."
  "2026-08-12T01:05:40.931Z","harness:codex","Implementation: provenance_value_domain_invalid remains in warnings and storage details but joins the advisory warning policy, so immutable historical pollution does not make health or strict exit fail. The documentation explicitly preserves write-time controlled-role validation and prohibits history rewriting as remediation."
  "2026-08-12T01:40:23.622Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: immutable legacy invalid provenance remains fully visible in health warnings/details but is advisory for the overall health boolean; new writes remain governed. Focused provenance and health suites passed 57 tests. Repository-wide coverage passed 486 files and 7,242 tests at exact 100% statements (52,343/52,343), branches (38,488/38,488), functions (10,770/10,770), and lines (50,579/50,579); lint, typecheck, contracts, security scan, and production audit passed."
